## Context
Child of tracker 1317 (forge leaks). Sites where a GitHub dependency may be legitimate:
measurement that joins Claude traces to GitHub PRs, review-evidence collection over the GitHub
GraphQL API, and a local GitHub Actions runner. The tracker says: decide per site, keep with a
reason or port. A keep decision with its reason recorded is a valid outcome.

Sites on main 2026-10-28:
- `scripts/trace-pr-join.py` (~66-87: `gh api` PR and comments)
- `scripts/trace_merge_path.py` (~7, ~40: a regex that recognises `gh pr merge` in traces)
- `scripts/review_evidence.py` (~505: `gh api graphql`)
- `scripts/local-ci.sh` (~101: `gh pr list`, plus the forge token passed to `act`)
- Not calls (pattern lists naming `gh`, keep): `scripts/census/exec-vs-mention.py`,
  `scripts/trace-wall-time.py`.

Parent: tracker 1317.

## Plan (raid f7fa41: Imagine, Blind-Spot, feasibility PASS)
Recommendation: keep all four, with a one-line reason comment at each call site and a log line.
- trace-pr-join.py ~80, ~87: GitHub PR and paginated comment measurement; a port would add a verb
  for one analytics script.
- trace_merge_path.py ~40: a regex over trace text, not a call.
- review_evidence.py ~505: GraphQL with pinned GitHub actor ids keyed by forge host; already uses
  forge.read_timeout and NET_ERR and fails closed; no-forge evidence goes through notes.
- local-ci.sh ~101: `act` is a GitHub Actions runner; it already skips forge-secret jobs when no
  forge (~89, ~167).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Each site above is either ported to `forge.py` (with a `none`-backend test: typed NOOP or
      refusal, never an empty all-clear) or recorded as keep-with-reason in this ticket's log
      and in a one-line comment at the call site
- [ ] Do not add a forge.py verb in this child unless a port needs it; a keep is preferred
      when the script's purpose is GitHub measurement
- [ ] `make check` passes
